pe":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\nThe ordinary worker still needed native request/journal responsibilities and a standalone immutable release installer. The prior 6994512 integration also exposed two real CI failures: a stale language inventory and complete cold qualification exceeding the unchanged 180-second deadline.\n\n## Changes\n- Integrates current main `5831f52`: complete nominal constructor, function and outer-program lowering, five selected owners and eleven HIA images.\n- Retains the HIA worker request and journal kernels and standalone release installer, with existing replay, unknown-outcome, refusal, identity and immutable-publication controls.\n- Repairs the source inventory/contract dependency order. Removes construction of an unused compiler CFG from the name oracle while preserving all 154 public assembly calls, 106 cases, 40 refusals and exact reference bytes.\n- Keeps all 46 generators, 16 nominal native modules, journal/request/install suites, the 180-second cold deadline, two cold workers, all 38 phases, fixed points and failure archive paths.\n- Preserves original failures, CI job logs, compiler/evidence archives and source-bound custody records. No deployed worker selection, active release or supported legacy owner is removed.\n\n## Frozen source\nHead: `4161e8d12d87906fde144f039da07908ad52d98a`  \nTree: `1c6ab0228f012429149997d1f731833739f433eb`  \nProfile: `selfhost-core-linux-x86_64-v65-native-journal-complete-nominal-lowering`  \n635 complete source/contract pins. Contract SHA-256: `30dd711b618a3c67c2ec841eb5f77eb64724f704b7c724bc12f4d2023a8ba533`.\n\n## Validation and limits\n- At the merged precursor `c4add225`, all 46 actual workflow generators reproduced all indexed bytes in 31.689 seconds; all 18 focused workflow/source/frame tests passed with identical loaded and executed IDs and zero anomalies.\n- The names-only repair separately passed 21 focused tests and kept the compiler HIA source byte-identical. Its local reference time changed from 7.15068 to 6.01871 seconds; this does not establish full cold performance.\n- Exact `6994512` source runs [42981052596](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/actions/runs/42981052596) and [42981060503](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/actions/runs/42981060503) failed: language inventory regeneration changed a semantic-support hash, and both cold jobs timed out with 34/38 completed phases. Both complete original archives and cleanup receipts remain retained. The PR synthetic merge had the exact same tree as the push source.\n- After the inventory repair, the original full source selection passed 317/317 tests on the explicitly recorded two-file repair state. This is not evidence for all later changes.\n- Exact `6994512` NDU workflow [42981060366](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/actions/runs/42981060366) passed independently.\n- Fixed desktop toolchains and all six external fixtures are ready; their receipts retain the original `6994512` build identity. New-source cold, native and full regression results are still pending and are not inferred from preparation or earlier passes.\n\nThe complete source inventory still contains 156 production Python modules. Whole HIA-native delivery, default activation, deployment and final legacy retirement remain open. Detailed scope and original observations: `docs/HIA_NATIVE_CLOSURE_20261111.md`, `docs/HIA_NATIVE_REWRITE_STATUS_20261111.md`, and `experiments/hia_v65_source_repair_20261111/`.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-11T04:59:46Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T08:53:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e0b22f1190121710c907ec96ef2c396b5cd12c06","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:codex/hia-native-closure-20261111-e26e","ref":"codex/hia-native-closure-20261111-e26e","repo":{"id":1432132756,"node_id":"R_kgDOVVyclA","name":"H